1
00:01:46,799 --> 00:01:47,519
It's short.

2
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:51,079
You're paying with gold?

3
00:01:51,599 --> 00:01:53,799
I remember I said before

4
00:01:53,799 --> 00:01:56,280
no virtual currency or Bitcoin.

5
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:57,000
Because I don't understand them.

6
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,680
But this gold doesn't have a certificate.

7
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:00,760
It's very easy to fake.

8
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:02,519
Can you just use cash next time?

9
00:02:02,719 --> 00:02:03,439
Fine.

10
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:07,040
I finally got Yang Awu and Ding Ning out of the way.

11
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:08,759
Can we hurry up and start?

12
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:12,000
Wait, how much is it per gram right now?

13
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:15,280
Go ahead.

14
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:16,639
You want to exploit legal loopholes

15
00:02:16,639 --> 00:02:18,159
to help the Fuxia Group.

16
00:02:18,159 --> 00:02:20,400
Your plan isn't meticulous or efficient enough.

17
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:21,120
You know that?

18
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:22,719
Then what should I do?

19
00:02:22,719 --> 00:02:25,280
Because sham litigation is a criminal offense.

20
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:27,400
The Supreme Court and Procuratorate are watching closely.

21
00:02:27,479 --> 00:02:28,080
I know.

22
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:31,000
You previously registered some small companies.

23
00:02:31,159 --> 00:02:32,400
Now I need you

24
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:34,120
to register more companies like those

25
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:36,319
to file hundreds of lawsuits.

26
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:38,960
Sure, I can do that.

27
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:39,639
Go on.

28
00:02:39,639 --> 00:02:41,000
The types of these lawsuits

29
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,520
should ideally be labor debt claims,

30
00:02:43,759 --> 00:02:44,879
divorce suits,

31
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:47,360
property-for-debt agreements, loan guarantees,

32
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:49,439
property preservation, and other minor cases.

33
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:51,879
They won't draw too much attention.

34
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:55,560
Actually, some inconspicuous clerical work

35
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:57,240
has already begun at our firm.

36
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,520
Xiao Zhou, distribute these cases to everyone.

37
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:00,919
Got it.

38
00:03:00,919 --> 00:03:01,719
My partner

39
00:03:01,719 --> 00:03:02,879
has already subtly

40
00:03:02,879 --> 00:03:04,800
used Rujie's intern lawyers

41
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:06,280
to complete the fundamental parts.

42
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:06,759
Good.

43
00:03:06,759 --> 00:03:09,240
Massive amounts of lawsuits require massive amounts of evidence.

44
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:11,439
So you need to forge large batches of IOUs,

45
00:03:11,479 --> 00:03:13,400
guarantee agreements, and video evidence.

46
00:03:13,919 --> 00:03:14,680
I understand.

47
00:03:15,439 --> 00:03:16,759
And with so many lawsuits,

48
00:03:16,759 --> 00:03:17,960
without a single client present,

49
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:19,879
all filed by representing lawyers,

50
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:22,120
it will raise suspicions at the court and procuratorate.

51
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:22,879
So?

52
00:03:22,879 --> 00:03:25,159
Those interns you recruited before

53
00:03:25,479 --> 00:03:27,159
were all kept in the dark.

54
00:03:27,159 --> 00:03:29,400
I need you to find some people

55
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,879
who are fully aware

56
00:03:30,879 --> 00:03:33,120
that they're participating in illegal activities.

57
00:03:33,199 --> 00:03:34,680
Because that's much more efficient.

58
00:03:37,159 --> 00:03:40,479
I've already set up a secret base.

59
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:44,280
I've carefully selected many veteran Fuxia employees.

60
00:03:44,719 --> 00:03:46,120
I told them that what they're doing

61
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:49,000
is like making fake cigarettes, liquor, or knockoff bags.

62
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:49,759
There's no difference.

63
00:03:50,039 --> 00:03:51,159
Even though it's illegal,

64
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:52,599
it doesn't hurt anyone.

65
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:54,960
Instead, it saves their own company.

66
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:58,479
This base's location had better be well-hidden.

67
00:03:58,800 --> 00:03:59,759
Don't worry.

68
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:03,479
I guarantee even you won't find it.

69
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:05,120
Good, good.

70
00:04:05,719 --> 00:04:07,280
What I mentioned earlier

71
00:04:07,319 --> 00:04:08,159
is going to be

72
00:04:08,159 --> 00:04:10,319
a massive workload for you.

73
00:04:10,919 --> 00:04:13,680
But I need you to finish all of it

74
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:16,680
before I go over to guide the case filings.

75
00:04:19,279 --> 00:04:20,079
Understood.

76
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:22,319
There's one more condition you must agree to.

77
00:04:23,079 --> 00:04:25,959
Ding Ning absolutely cannot be involved.

78
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:27,560
This is my bottom line.

79
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,600
You can't eat them all.

80
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,519
Only one at a time, got it?

81
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:34,199
The candy is good.

82
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:42,759
Awu is back.

83
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:47,120
What did you buy?

84
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:48,759
Grandpa, look.

85
00:04:48,759 --> 00:04:49,639
Coloring pens!

86
00:04:51,519 --> 00:04:51,959
Oh, right.

87
00:04:51,959 --> 00:04:53,279
I helped my friend's daughter

88
00:04:53,279 --> 00:04:54,240
organize a concert.

89
00:04:55,519 --> 00:04:57,160
Let's go listen to it together.

90
00:04:57,279 --> 00:04:58,120
OK.

91
00:04:58,240 --> 00:04:59,120
OK, here you go.

92
00:05:08,759 --> 00:05:09,879
I'll get going then.

93
00:05:10,959 --> 00:05:11,800
Dad is leaving.

94
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:18,439
Let me see.

95
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:21,600
A violin!

96
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,639
Have you seen one on TV before?

97
00:05:23,639 --> 00:05:24,079
Yes.

98
00:05:24,079 --> 00:05:24,839
Do you remember?

99
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:26,439
Let's go wash your hands.

100
00:05:26,439 --> 00:05:27,120
OK.

101
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:44,160
Not nervous.

102
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:45,600
I'm not nervous.

103
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:03,519
Look how fast those hands are moving!

104
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:11,399
Awu, does it sound good?

105
00:06:11,759 --> 00:06:12,600
Well, does it?

106
00:06:13,079 --> 00:06:14,839
The birdsong sounds better.

107
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:26,040
I really hate

108
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:27,759
this pretentious atmosphere.

109
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:30,079
But I love classical music.

110
00:06:30,639 --> 00:06:31,759
The first time it made me want to cry

111
00:06:31,759 --> 00:06:34,120
was at a small stall selling pirated CDs.

112
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:39,800
Bach's Well-Tempered Clavier Variations in G minor

113
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:42,879
always makes me feel like I can see

114
00:06:43,959 --> 00:06:45,439
the eyes of the natives,

115
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:48,160
and hear that quote from Churchill.

116
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,600
When Churchill was in his twenties,

117
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:52,360
in the Mamund Valley,

118
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:54,120
fighting the local natives...

119
00:06:54,399 --> 00:06:55,160
His comrade

120
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:57,319
got his eye shot out.

121
00:06:57,439 --> 00:06:59,399
An officer who was just joking around yesterday

122
00:06:59,399 --> 00:07:01,959
was hacked to pieces by the natives.

123
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:05,600
Well, why didn't they just stay home

124
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,079
instead of occupying other people's land?

125
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:10,560
The next day,

126
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:13,079
Churchill and his men entered the enemy village,

127
00:07:13,439 --> 00:07:15,800
burning houses, filling wells,

128
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:18,120
blowing up reservoirs, and destroying crops.

129
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:20,480
They made the natives hiding in the mountains

130
00:07:20,519 --> 00:07:23,360
watch helplessly as their homes were destroyed.

131
00:07:23,519 --> 00:07:25,319
Do you know what the eighty-year-old Churchill

132
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:27,399
concluded when looking back on this?

133
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:33,639
That those natives

134
00:07:33,639 --> 00:07:36,040
were at least happier than the prisoners in Auschwitz?

135
00:07:38,959 --> 00:07:39,720
No.

136
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:40,519
He said,

137
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:42,079
"Whether it was worth it,

138
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:43,759
I cannot say."

139
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:46,920
Then this isn't repenting.

140
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:48,480
People always hope that

141
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:50,079
those who have done bad things will repent,

142
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:52,240
and those who have committed crimes will be punished.

143
00:07:52,879 --> 00:07:55,879
But in reality, the people who actually do these things

144
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:58,360
never think about it that way.

145
00:08:00,839 --> 00:08:02,000
Then how do they think?

146
00:08:02,199 --> 00:08:04,040
Would a wolf, because of its own brutality,

147
00:08:04,279 --> 00:08:05,959
feel guilty toward its prey?

148
00:08:07,319 --> 00:08:08,079
No.

149
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:11,160
Repentance, punishment, reflection...

150
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:13,959
they won't make the world any less unjust

151
00:08:14,399 --> 00:08:15,319
or any less evil.

152
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:20,959
"Whether it was worth it,

153
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:22,600
I cannot say."

154
00:08:22,879 --> 00:08:27,079
That is the most sincere answer the person involved could give.

155
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,120
Good thing the law is there to make it clear for them.

156
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:35,120
The law isn't the only answer, either.

157
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:37,000
The speed at which it updates

158
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:39,679
doesn't necessarily keep up with the times.

159
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,559
Coming from a small place like Changyu Law Firm,

160
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,080
you probably haven't handled

161
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:46,600
a case on the scale of Fuxia Group, right?

162
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:48,720
To the point where even the CFO

163
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:50,440
has to be taken into custody.

164
00:08:51,159 --> 00:08:53,360
So this is a challenge for you.

165
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:56,759
Pulling me in as your assistant lawyer...

166
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:59,639
you handled that quite cleverly.

167
00:09:01,519 --> 00:09:03,720
Changyu Law Firm isn't a small place.

168
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:05,440
What I've seen...

169
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:07,559
you and those capitalists may not have.

170
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:09,559
Let's not keep taking cheap shots at each other.

171
00:09:09,759 --> 00:09:12,159
I like that sharp tongue of yours.

172
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:15,080
After all, only a newborn calf

173
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:17,559
is unafraid of tigers.

174
00:09:18,799 --> 00:09:19,559
However,

175
00:09:20,279 --> 00:09:23,080
all the resources at Rujie Law Firm are at your disposal.

176
00:09:25,559 --> 00:09:26,320
Also,

177
00:09:29,879 --> 00:09:30,720
this is for you.

178
00:09:32,679 --> 00:09:34,000
Parked at C105.

179
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:40,519
I thought it'd be a new phone.

180
00:09:43,639 --> 00:09:46,480
So, is gifting cars also Rujie's usual style?

181
00:10:21,679 --> 00:10:22,639
Thanks, Dad.

182
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:23,799
That's my girl.

183
00:10:39,559 --> 00:10:42,159
Thank you all for coming to my daughter's recital.

184
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:44,399
I specifically used my daughter's image

185
00:10:44,399 --> 00:10:46,559
to design a keychain

186
00:10:47,039 --> 00:10:48,639
as a gift for everyone.

187
00:10:48,879 --> 00:10:49,759
To keep as a memento.

188
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:50,919
A little souvenir.

189
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:52,440
Thank you. Thank you.

190
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:53,600
Thank you all.

191
00:11:40,159 --> 00:11:41,519
Fuxia Group

192
00:11:41,679 --> 00:11:43,960
is more than just a large enterprise.

193
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:45,720
It's the right-hand man for those people.

194
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:46,919
Just like Rujie.

195
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,919
Though I'm not in a position to know right now

196
00:11:48,919 --> 00:11:50,320
who those people are,

197
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:52,039
what I do know is that

198
00:11:52,679 --> 00:11:54,879
over the past dozen years, Fuxia Group

199
00:11:54,879 --> 00:11:57,639
has been secretly helping those people climb the ladder

200
00:11:57,639 --> 00:11:59,159
by providing financial support.

201
00:11:59,559 --> 00:12:01,720
Whether it's Zhao Yijie or Xu Ruqing,

202
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:02,840
it's not at all because

203
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:05,600
Fuxia Group is Rujie's client

204
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:06,320
that they're protecting it so fiercely.

205
00:12:06,639 --> 00:12:08,240
Covering up the existence of those people

206
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:10,720
has always been Zhao Yijie's true objective.

207
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:12,080
He sent you to find me.

208
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,480
You thought you were here to help me.

209
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:15,559
Zhao Yijie and those people will get me killed.

210
00:12:15,679 --> 00:12:16,519
And you too.

211
00:12:34,679 --> 00:12:36,840
Ding Ning, we meet again.

212
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:48,240
Heading home?

213
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,279
Good for you.

214
00:13:06,919 --> 00:13:08,360
Joined a new company,

215
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:09,720
got a new boss,

216
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:11,320
someone gave you a new car.

217
00:13:12,039 --> 00:13:14,000
Starting a new chapter in life.

218
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:14,960
Congratulations.

219
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:18,440
I just took a case, that's all.

220
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:19,480
Is this really necessary?

221
00:13:20,679 --> 00:13:22,159
If you wanted to change firms,

222
00:13:22,679 --> 00:13:25,000
there are countless firms out there.

223
00:13:25,279 --> 00:13:26,639
Did you have to choose Rujie?

224
00:13:26,639 --> 00:13:28,320
What do you mean I had to?

225
00:13:28,759 --> 00:13:29,639
It's not like you don't know.

226
00:13:29,639 --> 00:13:31,639
I was kicked out for reporting you.

227
00:13:31,919 --> 00:13:33,399
If it weren't a firm the size of Rujie,

228
00:13:33,399 --> 00:13:34,480
who would dare take me?

229
00:13:34,519 --> 00:13:35,960
Then why did you tell Zhao Yijie

230
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:37,159
instead of telling me?

231
00:13:37,399 --> 00:13:38,879
If you were changing firms,

232
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:41,320
I could've recommended you.

233
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:42,440
Understand?

234
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:43,120
Really?

235
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:45,000
How would you even make that call?

236
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:45,919
Would you tell them,

237
00:13:45,919 --> 00:13:47,039
"The lawyer I want to recommend

238
00:13:47,039 --> 00:13:47,960
is the one who reported me

239
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:48,960
for having Alzheimer's"?

240
00:13:50,159 --> 00:13:51,279
What a joke.

241
00:13:51,279 --> 00:13:51,840
Then let me ask you,

242
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:53,039
how long have you been

243
00:13:53,039 --> 00:13:54,480
in the legal profession?

244
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:55,639
Don't you know

245
00:13:55,639 --> 00:13:58,120
how deep the waters run at Rujie?

246
00:13:58,120 --> 00:13:59,080
Fine, let's leave that aside.

247
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:00,720
How many times have I warned you

248
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:02,639
to stay away from big corporate cases?

249
00:14:02,639 --> 00:14:04,799
Wait, what's wrong with corporate cases?

250
00:14:04,919 --> 00:14:06,120
Do you actually believe

251
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,720
that wealth itself is evil,

252
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:09,240
and all the ways to get rich are in the penal code?

253
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:10,120
You believe that nonsense?

254
00:14:10,159 --> 00:14:11,919
What is it with you young people?

255
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:12,639
I say one word,

256
00:14:12,639 --> 00:14:14,600
and you have twenty waiting for me.

257
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:17,240
Yu Xiaoyue is like this, and so are you.

258
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:18,960
Because I'm sick of being controlled!

259
00:14:23,799 --> 00:14:25,440
Does controlling me make you feel secure?

260
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:27,919
If you use "for my own good"

261
00:14:27,919 --> 00:14:28,879
as an excuse to make me listen to you,

262
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:30,480
then how are you any different

263
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:31,440
from my parents or my mentor?

264
00:14:34,039 --> 00:14:34,639
Grandpa,

265
00:14:36,279 --> 00:14:37,360
I need to poop.

266
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:54,559
I'm worried about you.

267
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:56,960
You went to a completely unfamiliar place

268
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:58,440
and took on such a huge case.

269
00:14:59,279 --> 00:15:01,000
But you don't have a single ally.

270
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:03,200
That's why I brought Zhao Yijie in.

271
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:04,320
What better ally could there be

272
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:06,759
than the person you should be most wary of?

273
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:08,600
Whether Liang Zidong is playing dumb

274
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:09,519
to set me up,

275
00:15:09,519 --> 00:15:11,559
or if Zhao Yijie is actually being sincere,

276
00:15:11,799 --> 00:15:13,360
I can't trust anyone right now.

277
00:15:13,799 --> 00:15:14,440
And...

278
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:15,039
I...

279
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:16,440
I know better than you do

280
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:18,799
that everyone wants to make me the scapegoat.

281
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:19,679
So it's not like

282
00:15:19,679 --> 00:15:21,039
I just do whatever Liang Zidong tells me,

283
00:15:21,039 --> 00:15:22,679
nor does Zhao Yijie giving me a car

284
00:15:22,679 --> 00:15:23,919
mean he controls me.

285
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:26,240
Are you Liang Zidong's representing lawyer right now?

286
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:27,200
In this case,

287
00:15:27,279 --> 00:15:29,879
you're the one signing all the documents, right?

288
00:15:30,039 --> 00:15:30,919
So if something goes wrong,

289
00:15:30,919 --> 00:15:32,679
you'll be the first one arrested, not Zhao Yijie.

290
00:15:32,679 --> 00:15:34,720
Nor anyone else. Do you understand?

291
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:36,480
Zhao Yijie signed them too.

292
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:37,080
So what?

293
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:38,759
You're the representing lawyer for this case.

294
00:15:38,759 --> 00:15:40,080
He's just an assistant lawyer.

295
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:41,039
What responsibility does he have?

296
00:15:41,039 --> 00:15:42,000
He's my boss.

297
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,240
Do you think he can get away with it?

298
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:47,840
Who's the hunter and who's the prey...

299
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:49,080
that's still up in the air.

300
00:15:49,799 --> 00:15:51,399
He won't always be at the top of the food chain.

301
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:53,039
There's always a bigger predator lurking.

302
00:15:58,480 --> 00:15:59,159
Alright.

303
00:16:00,759 --> 00:16:02,320
What did Liang Zidong tell you?

304
00:16:07,559 --> 00:16:08,799
He told me to find some sort of...

305
00:16:09,519 --> 00:16:10,919
Sham Litigation Base.

306
00:16:14,159 --> 00:16:16,720
What Sham Litigation Base? What is that?

307
00:16:18,279 --> 00:16:19,279
Never mind. Stay out of it.

308
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:21,840
Are you going to the hospital tomorrow morning or afternoon?

309
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:22,639
Do you want me to come with you?

310
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:24,519
No need. I can go by myself.

311
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:25,679
Really.

312
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:28,679
Alright. I'll leave you to it.

313
00:16:32,159 --> 00:16:34,240
Just be careful with everything, okay?

314
00:16:44,879 --> 00:16:45,679
Mr. Bi,

315
00:16:45,679 --> 00:16:47,279
just as you instructed,

316
00:16:47,279 --> 00:16:48,399
we bypassed Zhao Yijie.

317
00:16:48,399 --> 00:16:50,159
He doesn't know anything right now.

318
00:16:50,159 --> 00:16:50,879
Ruqing,

319
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,399
you and Yijie have been with me for 15 years, haven't you?

320
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:54,240
Yes.

321
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:56,480
You two have different personalities.

322
00:16:57,039 --> 00:16:59,559
I can reason with you on some things,

323
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:01,360
but not necessarily with Yijie.

324
00:17:01,559 --> 00:17:03,240
But I still have to say something

325
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:04,559
you might not like to hear.

326
00:17:05,559 --> 00:17:07,200
Mr. Bi, please speak your mind.

327
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:08,480
There's nothing I wouldn't want to hear.

328
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:09,279
I know.

329
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:11,319
Zhao Yijie is indeed more capable than me.

330
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,119
Over the years,

331
00:17:12,119 --> 00:17:13,519
we've managed to stay safe,

332
00:17:13,519 --> 00:17:15,160
and he actually deserves the most credit.

333
00:17:15,319 --> 00:17:16,440
So I'm worried

334
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:18,440
that if I team up with Liang Zidong this time

335
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:20,680
to destroy the Sham Litigation Base

336
00:17:20,799 --> 00:17:22,240
and the future of Fuxia Group,

337
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:24,119
it will completely devastate Yijie.

338
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:24,759
Mr. Bi,

339
00:17:24,759 --> 00:17:26,839
I don't think he'll be completely devastated.

340
00:17:26,839 --> 00:17:30,079
But Fuxia Group is indeed

341
00:17:30,240 --> 00:17:32,640
what Yijie cares about most.

342
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:34,759
He might be very disheartened.

343
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:41,400
That female lawyer of Liang Zidong's,

344
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:42,359
what's the deal with her?

345
00:17:43,319 --> 00:17:45,160
You mean Ding Ning?

346
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:45,720
Yes.

347
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:48,799
This woman's appearance

348
00:17:49,079 --> 00:17:50,200
is indeed unexpected.

349
00:17:50,519 --> 00:17:53,480
Can you guarantee she'll play along

350
00:17:53,599 --> 00:17:56,039
and go report it as planned?

351
00:17:57,759 --> 00:17:58,519
Mr. Bi, here's the thing.

352
00:17:58,519 --> 00:18:00,119
This woman is quite unusual.

353
00:18:00,119 --> 00:18:00,640
I think

354
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:03,440
it'll be hard to use conventional threats or bribes

355
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:04,319
to keep her in line.

356
00:18:04,319 --> 00:18:05,119
But,

357
00:18:06,079 --> 00:18:08,240
I don't think there will be any major issues.

358
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:09,279
Sounds like

359
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:12,079
you're not very confident.

360
00:18:13,279 --> 00:18:14,079
Mr. Bi,

361
00:18:14,839 --> 00:18:16,200
I will definitely do my best.

362
00:19:09,559 --> 00:19:12,079
Hello, friend.

363
00:19:17,119 --> 00:19:18,920
Not enthusiastic at all.

364
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:27,200
Mr. Zhao.

365
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:28,519
Mr. Zhao. Mr. Zhao. Mr. Zhao.

366
00:19:30,119 --> 00:19:30,880
Come on.

367
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:34,359
Let me introduce everyone to...

368
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,039
Yu Songfan.

369
00:19:36,279 --> 00:19:38,519
The famous Judge Yu.

370
00:19:41,519 --> 00:19:43,240
Show some appreciation. Come on.

371
00:19:48,119 --> 00:19:48,720
All right.

372
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:51,000
We're tight on time. Let's begin.

373
00:19:51,519 --> 00:19:52,400
Financial claims.

374
00:19:53,319 --> 00:19:55,359
The commerce and relevant departments'

375
00:19:55,359 --> 00:19:56,480
registration numbers on my end are ready.

376
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:58,519
Filing the cases for these lawsuits

377
00:19:58,519 --> 00:19:59,960
will be a bit more difficult for two of them.

378
00:20:00,359 --> 00:20:01,519
As for the judges in the filing division,

379
00:20:01,519 --> 00:20:02,440
I looked into them.

380
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:06,839
These three judges won't work.

381
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,240
Then what does Ms. Yu suggest?

382
00:20:10,319 --> 00:20:12,079
We're not picking judges right now.

383
00:20:13,039 --> 00:20:14,039
This court

384
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:16,720
is especially good at catching

385
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:17,799
the sham litigation you are currently doing.

386
00:20:18,200 --> 00:20:20,319
They once sent judges from their court

387
00:20:20,319 --> 00:20:22,640
to give presentations at other district courts

388
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:23,880
to share their experience.

389
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:25,400
Didn't you investigate this?

390
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:26,880
So it's best

391
00:20:26,880 --> 00:20:28,920
that you transfer to the Dongning District Court.

392
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:32,640
Listen to Judge Yu.

393
00:20:36,559 --> 00:20:37,319
Next.

394
00:20:37,839 --> 00:20:38,920
The property-for-debt agreement.

395
00:20:39,079 --> 00:20:40,240
The video is already done.

396
00:20:40,559 --> 00:20:43,000
Since the jurisdiction is basically set,

397
00:20:43,279 --> 00:20:45,960
the cases are mainly in the West District Court.

398
00:20:46,599 --> 00:20:47,720
The West District Court is fine.

399
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:50,200
But they must be submitted within three months.

400
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:53,039
Because personnel changes are frequent at this court,

401
00:20:53,039 --> 00:20:55,480
the ones taking these cases are all young judges.

402
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:56,559
As long as the case is filed,

403
00:20:56,839 --> 00:20:58,400
there basically won't be any surprises.

404
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:00,559
Good.

405
00:21:01,799 --> 00:21:03,119
Hello. Long time no see.

406
00:21:03,279 --> 00:21:03,839
Yes, yes.

407
00:21:03,839 --> 00:21:06,119
Right, I forgot to tell you.

408
00:21:06,599 --> 00:21:08,720
Kong has helped me for many years.

409
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:10,559
Really? We've known each other for years too.

410
00:21:12,079 --> 00:21:13,920
That concert he gifted to your daughter

411
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:15,079
was a huge success.

412
00:21:16,319 --> 00:21:17,279
Those math test papers

413
00:21:17,279 --> 00:21:19,440
were also sneaked into my court for you by Kong.

414
00:21:19,440 --> 00:21:19,920
Right?

415
00:21:19,920 --> 00:21:22,119
All right. Why do you still hold a grudge?

416
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:23,920
Here's the deal.

417
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:25,880
This evidence is crucial.

418
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:26,839
So I'll handle it.

419
00:21:26,839 --> 00:21:28,759
As for the rest, the divorce lawsuits,

420
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:30,839
loan guarantees, and collective home purchases,

421
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:32,119
we'll review them later.

422
00:21:32,519 --> 00:21:32,799
Okay.

423
00:21:32,799 --> 00:21:34,480
You guys get back to work, okay?

424
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:38,039
Take care, Mr. Zhao.

425
00:21:45,359 --> 00:21:46,119
Zhao Yijie.

426
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:47,599
I need to tell you something.

427
00:21:48,039 --> 00:21:49,599
I want to raise the price.

428
00:21:49,599 --> 00:21:51,680
Double the price, and give it to me ASAP.

429
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:52,960
Are you crazy?

430
00:21:53,319 --> 00:21:55,279
You're blatantly raising the price on the spot.

431
00:21:55,839 --> 00:21:57,480
You can negotiate.

432
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:58,680
But I need it as soon as possible.

433
00:21:58,920 --> 00:22:00,000
I need it next week.

434
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:00,920
Next week?

435
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:01,799
Yes. Yes.

436
00:22:03,079 --> 00:22:04,640
Are you trying to run away with Yang Awu again?

437
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,440
Where could we go?

438
00:22:05,440 --> 00:22:06,079
Didn't you say

439
00:22:06,079 --> 00:22:07,880
you could find me no matter where we go?

440
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:11,359
Just tell me, can you pay it or not?

441
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:20,480
Then tell me first what you actually need it for.

442
00:22:21,119 --> 00:22:22,000
Think about it clearly.

443
00:22:22,480 --> 00:22:24,400
You can't spend money recklessly.

444
00:22:24,759 --> 00:22:26,359
It'll easily get us targeted.

445
00:22:28,960 --> 00:22:31,000
I need to leave some money for Yang Awu.

446
00:22:31,519 --> 00:22:32,839
Why do you need it next week?

447
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:36,559
Because next week I'll be done with all my tasks.

448
00:22:36,799 --> 00:22:37,960
I want the money in advance.

449
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:40,000
I don't trust you, okay?

450
00:22:41,119 --> 00:22:42,519
Also, I want to compensate someone.

451
00:22:44,759 --> 00:22:45,440
Who?

452
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:47,000
Yang Miao.

453
00:22:47,640 --> 00:22:48,799
Yang Cheng's daughter.

454
00:22:50,799 --> 00:22:51,920
I want to compensate her.

455
00:22:55,720 --> 00:22:57,000
So give it to me ASAP.

456
00:22:57,440 --> 00:22:58,960
Otherwise, I won't work for you.

457
00:23:22,599 --> 00:23:24,400
No thanks. Let's talk business.

458
00:23:25,079 --> 00:23:27,400
Alright. Then give it to me straight.

459
00:23:27,400 --> 00:23:28,799
Asking me out alone.

460
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:29,759
What is it about?

461
00:23:29,759 --> 00:23:31,359
We're all adults here.

462
00:23:31,359 --> 00:23:34,240
Let's not play dumb, alright?

463
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:37,039
I know there's someone backing you.

464
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:37,960
And...

465
00:23:37,960 --> 00:23:39,519
the person backing you...

466
00:23:39,519 --> 00:23:42,559
regarding the Sham Litigation Base...

467
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:44,640
bypassed Zhao Yijie.

468
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:53,640
What makes you so sure?

469
00:23:54,039 --> 00:23:56,200
I've been a judge for half my life.

470
00:23:56,920 --> 00:23:59,240
I obviously have my own sources.

471
00:24:08,359 --> 00:24:09,400
What do you want?

472
00:24:14,079 --> 00:24:15,480
Actually, we all have

473
00:24:15,480 --> 00:24:17,000
people and things that matter to us.

474
00:24:18,039 --> 00:24:19,000
At this moment,

475
00:24:19,799 --> 00:24:22,559
the most important to me is my grandson, Yang Awu.

476
00:24:23,279 --> 00:24:24,480
But I know that

477
00:24:24,519 --> 00:24:26,680
with you behind Zhao Yijie,

478
00:24:27,039 --> 00:24:31,160
I can never truly reunite with my grandson.

479
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:34,079
I get it.

480
00:24:35,480 --> 00:24:42,759
You want us to change the adoption papers for you.

481
00:24:43,039 --> 00:24:43,680
Yes.

482
00:24:44,559 --> 00:24:47,440
I want to officially adopt this child.

483
00:24:47,799 --> 00:24:50,559
Judge Yu really lives by "if you can't beat them, join them."

484
00:24:50,759 --> 00:24:51,319
Suit yourself.

485
00:24:51,319 --> 00:24:52,680
But what makes you think

486
00:24:52,759 --> 00:24:53,519
I would betray

487
00:24:53,519 --> 00:24:56,200
my long-time partner, Zhao Yijie,

488
00:24:56,319 --> 00:24:59,200
to pass a message to my superiors for you?

489
00:24:59,480 --> 00:25:00,559
Because I am certain

490
00:25:01,920 --> 00:25:03,319
that on this matter,

491
00:25:03,319 --> 00:25:06,039
you and Zhao Yijie don't see eye to eye.

492
00:25:06,640 --> 00:25:07,279
Enough.

493
00:25:07,920 --> 00:25:09,920
Xu, how many times have I told you?

494
00:25:10,160 --> 00:25:11,680
Regarding the Sham Litigation Base,

495
00:25:11,680 --> 00:25:13,359
stay out of it.

496
00:25:13,759 --> 00:25:14,839
If anything does happen,

497
00:25:14,839 --> 00:25:16,359
I'll explain it to him, okay?

498
00:25:16,680 --> 00:25:17,759
The most important thing for you right now

499
00:25:17,759 --> 00:25:19,359
is to get what I need ready.

500
00:25:20,200 --> 00:25:21,400
I know there are risks.

501
00:25:21,400 --> 00:25:22,880
But of course we must protect Fuxia.

502
00:25:23,160 --> 00:25:23,720
Xu.

503
00:25:24,319 --> 00:25:26,079
I'm not afraid. Why are you?

504
00:25:29,640 --> 00:25:30,440
And another thing,

505
00:25:30,440 --> 00:25:34,400
I can get Ding Ning to report the Sham Litigation Base.

506
00:25:36,799 --> 00:25:37,799
So tell me,

507
00:25:38,759 --> 00:25:42,880
if the Sham Litigation Base gets busted,

508
00:25:44,839 --> 00:25:46,400
wouldn't you go down with it?

509
00:25:47,400 --> 00:25:51,200
You think Zhao Yijie is the only one who knows how to escape?

510
00:25:55,799 --> 00:25:57,039
Once the report is successful,

511
00:25:57,039 --> 00:25:58,000
you need to give me

512
00:25:58,000 --> 00:25:59,319
what I need.

513
00:26:02,160 --> 00:26:03,559
One more thing.

514
00:26:03,720 --> 00:26:05,559
After this whole thing is over,

515
00:26:06,240 --> 00:26:08,519
Ding Ning must get out unscathed.

516
00:26:12,119 --> 00:26:13,039
Let's wait and see.

517
00:26:22,119 --> 00:26:23,599
Stop fussing, okay? We'll find it later.

518
00:26:23,599 --> 00:26:24,160
How did this happen?

519
00:26:24,160 --> 00:26:25,119
Take care of him. Take care of him.

520
00:26:25,119 --> 00:26:26,240
Let's sign this first.

521
00:26:26,359 --> 00:26:27,240
Wait a sec, wait a sec.

522
00:26:27,240 --> 00:26:28,559
Sorry, sorry. I'm so sorry.

523
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:30,079
You know these two kids,

524
00:26:30,079 --> 00:26:31,359
how hard they are for us to handle?

525
00:26:31,640 --> 00:26:32,799
We'll go in a bit, okay?

526
00:26:32,880 --> 00:26:34,440
Let me get you one of those, alright?

527
00:26:37,480 --> 00:26:38,319
Zhou Hao.

528
00:26:39,480 --> 00:26:40,200
Here, here.

529
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:41,759
He peed his pants.

530
00:26:41,759 --> 00:26:42,680
Let me hold you.

531
00:26:46,759 --> 00:26:47,680
This one. This is fine.

532
00:26:47,880 --> 00:26:48,799
Up we go!

533
00:26:48,799 --> 00:26:50,160
Thanks. Thank you.

534
00:26:52,759 --> 00:26:53,519
Alright.

535
00:26:53,559 --> 00:26:54,799
If there's any progress later on,

536
00:26:54,799 --> 00:26:55,759
we'll keep in touch.

537
00:26:55,759 --> 00:26:56,359
Okay, okay.

538
00:26:56,359 --> 00:26:57,119
Thanks. Thank you.

539
00:26:57,599 --> 00:26:58,400
Lawyer Ding.

540
00:27:03,599 --> 00:27:04,359
Lawyer Ding.

541
00:27:04,359 --> 00:27:05,640
Come, this way.

542
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:09,000
Our financial director's case,

543
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:10,720
is your team handling it?

544
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:14,039
What are you afraid of?

545
00:27:14,160 --> 00:27:15,440
Lawyer Ding is one of us.

546
00:27:15,519 --> 00:27:16,160
Right?

547
00:27:17,359 --> 00:27:18,160
Normally,

548
00:27:18,160 --> 00:27:19,400
whoever pays more

549
00:27:19,480 --> 00:27:21,599
gets their case handled with more care.

550
00:27:21,720 --> 00:27:23,079
There's nothing wrong with that logic.

551
00:27:24,279 --> 00:27:25,079
Don't worry.

552
00:27:25,200 --> 00:27:27,160
We take it just as seriously, regardless of the pay.

553
00:27:27,599 --> 00:27:29,000
I didn't mean it like that.

554
00:27:29,079 --> 00:27:29,880
I meant,

555
00:27:30,200 --> 00:27:31,759
for Liang Zidong's case,

556
00:27:31,759 --> 00:27:33,480
you really don't need to put in extra effort.

557
00:27:35,039 --> 00:27:36,119
Among us,

558
00:27:36,119 --> 00:27:38,079
we have a WeChat group for family members.

559
00:27:39,799 --> 00:27:41,359
Back when Mr. Liang went missing,

560
00:27:41,359 --> 00:27:43,039
we were all very worried.

561
00:27:43,119 --> 00:27:45,279
But Mrs. Liang acted like nothing happened.

562
00:27:45,279 --> 00:27:46,440
We were quite confused.

563
00:27:46,599 --> 00:27:47,799
Only later did we find out

564
00:27:48,440 --> 00:27:51,000
that she has connections in the Procuratorate.

565
00:27:51,240 --> 00:27:52,640
She didn't need to worry at all.

566
00:27:53,400 --> 00:27:54,160
You know?

567
00:27:57,359 --> 00:27:58,799
It was most likely an attempted kidnapping.

568
00:27:59,720 --> 00:28:00,920
It scares me just thinking about it.

569
00:28:03,119 --> 00:28:04,680
I mean, stealing is one thing,

570
00:28:04,880 --> 00:28:06,480
but my dad has been paralyzed in bed for years,

571
00:28:06,559 --> 00:28:08,119
and they still pushed him out and put him through all that.

572
00:28:08,680 --> 00:28:10,240
If anything happened to my dad,

573
00:28:10,240 --> 00:28:11,799
what would we children do?

574
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:14,400
Please calm down first.

575
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:16,440
We've already recorded the basic facts in the statement.

576
00:28:16,880 --> 00:28:18,559
But according to the statement,

577
00:28:18,680 --> 00:28:20,720
it seems only your family suffered financial loss.

578
00:28:23,759 --> 00:28:26,400
You said they pushed the old man outside,

579
00:28:26,640 --> 00:28:28,759
and your family is missing 2,000 yuan.

580
00:28:29,319 --> 00:28:30,680
But your older brother said 5,000 was missing.

581
00:28:33,640 --> 00:28:36,119
M-maybe I was just anxious at the time

582
00:28:36,480 --> 00:28:37,480
and remembered it wrong.

583
00:28:38,160 --> 00:28:40,880
It's 2,000 missing, not 5,000.

584
00:28:44,880 --> 00:28:46,000
Look how frantic we were.

585
00:28:49,160 --> 00:28:50,160
It's okay now, Dad.

586
00:28:50,599 --> 00:28:51,319
Oh, right.

587
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:53,160
There's one more thing.

588
00:28:53,440 --> 00:28:54,440
It doesn't belong to my dad.

589
00:28:54,519 --> 00:28:55,240
Look.

590
00:28:56,960 --> 00:28:59,119
On that day at the police station entrance,

591
00:28:59,480 --> 00:29:00,720
it was around my dad's neck.

592
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:02,200
I've asked around,

593
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:03,279
and it doesn't belong to our family.

594
00:29:07,160 --> 00:29:08,640
I'm not making this up.

595
00:29:08,759 --> 00:29:09,519
There was this one time,

596
00:29:10,240 --> 00:29:12,599
Mr. Liang kept saying he was working overtime,

597
00:29:12,599 --> 00:29:14,240
but he wasn't at the company.

598
00:29:14,240 --> 00:29:15,240
Mrs. Liang, well,

599
00:29:15,240 --> 00:29:16,839
she was worried he was cheating.

600
00:29:16,839 --> 00:29:18,839
She even asked our Old Lin to write some code

601
00:29:18,839 --> 00:29:20,240
to track his location.

602
00:29:20,240 --> 00:29:21,519
And guess what?

603
00:29:21,920 --> 00:29:23,799
He was talking business at a bar.

604
00:29:23,920 --> 00:29:25,079
The people drinking with him

605
00:29:25,279 --> 00:29:26,559
were all big shots.

606
00:29:27,119 --> 00:29:28,000
So, you see,

607
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:29,599
Mr. Liang's case

608
00:29:29,640 --> 00:29:31,680
is much simpler than ours.

609
00:29:31,680 --> 00:29:34,799
He knows people who can protect him.

610
00:29:38,559 --> 00:29:39,880
Excuse me, I need to take this.

611
00:29:39,880 --> 00:29:40,799
No problem at all.

612
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:45,200
Hello, Chairman Fan.

613
00:29:45,799 --> 00:29:46,880
Is it convenient to meet up?

614
00:30:01,519 --> 00:30:02,319
Have you been waiting long?

615
00:30:02,519 --> 00:30:03,079
It's fine.

616
00:30:11,640 --> 00:30:13,640
Do you remember that drug dealer you saved?

617
00:30:14,119 --> 00:30:15,359
I didn't save him.

618
00:30:15,839 --> 00:30:17,799
I just gave his lawyer some advice.

619
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:19,279
There's a joint investigation by three countries

620
00:30:19,279 --> 00:30:20,279
into a transnational drug trafficking case.

621
00:30:20,279 --> 00:30:22,079
Thanks to the clues provided by this dealer,

622
00:30:22,759 --> 00:30:23,640
the case was solved.

623
00:30:23,839 --> 00:30:24,880
The Ministry even specifically commended

624
00:30:24,880 --> 00:30:26,000
the drug dealer's lawyer.

625
00:30:28,279 --> 00:30:28,920
That's great.

626
00:30:33,400 --> 00:30:35,519
You sent all those supplements, right?

627
00:30:38,119 --> 00:30:39,599
I brought them all back to your parents.

628
00:30:41,319 --> 00:30:42,400
Actually, when you're not home,

629
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:44,400
your parents talk about you a lot.

630
00:30:45,359 --> 00:30:47,640
Your dad always brings you up when he drinks.

631
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:49,920
And your mom constantly worries about you.

632
00:30:50,079 --> 00:30:51,400
She told me to come check on you often.

633
00:30:57,920 --> 00:30:59,359
Are they both doing okay?

634
00:30:59,519 --> 00:31:00,319
They're doing great.

635
00:31:00,839 --> 00:31:02,559
I go back and check on them every few days.

636
00:31:09,759 --> 00:31:12,400
By the way, that vajra pendant I gave you...

637
00:31:12,599 --> 00:31:13,480
do you still have it?

638
00:31:19,400 --> 00:31:21,319
I was just about to tell you about that.

639
00:31:21,319 --> 00:31:22,680
You're in court all the time,

640
00:31:22,759 --> 00:31:24,119
so it's not convenient to wear jewelry.

641
00:31:29,599 --> 00:31:31,359
Why are you suddenly asking about it?

642
00:31:31,680 --> 00:31:33,400
There's a burglary case.

643
00:31:33,400 --> 00:31:35,200
I saw a new piece of evidence today.

644
00:31:35,240 --> 00:31:36,319
It was a vajra pendant.

645
00:31:36,759 --> 00:31:37,759
I was just thinking

646
00:31:37,920 --> 00:31:39,359
it looked a lot like the one I gave you.

647
00:31:41,359 --> 00:31:43,039
But you can buy these things anywhere.

648
00:31:43,079 --> 00:31:44,480
So it might not be the one I gave you.

649
00:31:53,640 --> 00:31:54,480
You don't have to hide it.

650
00:31:55,160 --> 00:31:56,400
The guys watching Liang Zidong

651
00:31:56,480 --> 00:31:57,920
are my colleagues from another team.

652
00:31:59,680 --> 00:32:01,799
I also wanted to talk to you about this today.

653
00:32:05,920 --> 00:32:06,720
Someone asked me a favor.

654
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:08,519
This is from the guy who hurt you.

655
00:32:09,039 --> 00:32:10,119
A new phone to replace yours.

656
00:32:10,759 --> 00:32:12,440
He originally wanted to meet up with you,

657
00:32:12,559 --> 00:32:13,759
but you didn't reply to his messages.

658
00:32:17,960 --> 00:32:19,599
And here I thought you actually came to see me.

659
00:32:20,680 --> 00:32:21,519
Of course.

660
00:32:21,880 --> 00:32:23,000
I wanted to see you.

661
00:32:23,599 --> 00:32:24,839
But considering how busy you are,

662
00:32:24,920 --> 00:32:27,079
I figured it'd be better to save things up and see you at once.

663
00:32:28,759 --> 00:32:29,799
Don't get me wrong.

664
00:32:29,799 --> 00:32:31,240
I'm pretty mad at him too.

665
00:32:31,440 --> 00:32:33,599
But he really is a very responsible cop.

666
00:32:34,960 --> 00:32:36,440
I'm not trying to defend him.

667
00:32:36,480 --> 00:32:38,720
Their captain has already criticized and warned him.

668
00:32:39,319 --> 00:32:41,640
But lately I've heard he's going to be disciplined.

669
00:32:41,799 --> 00:32:43,279
He wasn't targeting you, Ding Ning.

670
00:32:43,559 --> 00:32:45,599
Could you write a letter of forgiveness for him?

671
00:32:45,799 --> 00:32:47,480
Besides, you're so strong.

672
00:32:47,480 --> 00:32:48,440
I'm strong?

673
00:32:50,400 --> 00:32:51,039
No.

674
00:32:52,359 --> 00:32:54,119
Is being strong really a virtue?

675
00:32:56,240 --> 00:32:57,759
I had a conflict with your colleague,

676
00:32:58,720 --> 00:32:59,960
and you didn't even ask how my injuries are.

677
00:32:59,960 --> 00:33:01,359
You only thought about pleading for him,

678
00:33:01,359 --> 00:33:02,240
asking me to forgive him,

679
00:33:02,440 --> 00:33:03,640
so things wouldn't blow out of proportion.

680
00:33:04,440 --> 00:33:06,319
And you know I'll definitely back down,

681
00:33:06,759 --> 00:33:07,400
right?

682
00:33:10,599 --> 00:33:11,480
So, you see...

683
00:33:12,880 --> 00:33:14,519
where does being strong get me in the end?

684
00:33:16,839 --> 00:33:18,759
I see all of you being so loyal and righteous,

685
00:33:18,759 --> 00:33:19,680
brave, and just.

686
00:33:21,240 --> 00:33:22,039
But what about me?

687
00:33:23,160 --> 00:33:24,119
That's not true.

688
00:33:24,480 --> 00:33:25,359
I just wanted to say...

689
00:33:25,359 --> 00:33:26,160
thank you.

690
00:33:28,359 --> 00:33:30,160
This way, I don't have to feel so guilty anymore.

691
00:33:33,319 --> 00:33:34,079
Guilty?

692
00:33:37,359 --> 00:33:38,359
It's my fault.

693
00:33:39,279 --> 00:33:40,960
I should have managed my expectations better,

694
00:33:42,720 --> 00:33:44,319
so that none of you could ever hurt me again.

695
00:33:48,240 --> 00:33:48,920
Ding Ning.

696
00:33:49,680 --> 00:33:50,400
Ding Ning!

697
00:33:57,039 --> 00:33:57,680
Any updates?

698
00:33:58,359 --> 00:33:59,920
Any news from Ding Ning?

699
00:34:00,079 --> 00:34:01,039
She goes to work during the day,

700
00:34:01,160 --> 00:34:02,240
meets friends at night,

701
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:04,279
or goes back to Yu Songfan's place.

702
00:34:04,599 --> 00:34:06,839
Either way, she hasn't gone looking for the Sham Litigation Base.

703
00:34:07,599 --> 00:34:10,320
Alright. Let me know if there's any new information.

704
00:34:10,679 --> 00:34:11,400
Thank you.

705
00:34:15,800 --> 00:34:16,599
Everyone,

706
00:34:18,760 --> 00:34:19,559
our team

707
00:34:20,159 --> 00:34:21,840
was originally led by the Provincial Supervisory Commission,

708
00:34:22,519 --> 00:34:24,840
joining forces with the Municipal Public Security Bureau and Procuratorate,

709
00:34:26,320 --> 00:34:27,519
starting our investigation with Fuxia Group,

710
00:34:28,760 --> 00:34:31,559
and tracking down their protective umbrella step by step.

711
00:34:32,880 --> 00:34:34,719
It's been two years now.

712
00:34:35,119 --> 00:34:36,239
We've reviewed over ten thousand files,

713
00:34:36,760 --> 00:34:38,519
and questioned over a thousand people.

714
00:34:38,800 --> 00:34:41,039
We've already gathered a massive amount of criminal evidence.

715
00:34:41,199 --> 00:34:41,840
Now,

716
00:34:42,440 --> 00:34:44,639
we've also gathered inside information from Liang Zidong.

717
00:34:45,400 --> 00:34:46,840
It's time to close the net.

718
00:34:47,360 --> 00:34:47,880
Deputy Team Leader,

719
00:34:48,440 --> 00:34:49,960
we got the intel from Liang Zidong

720
00:34:49,960 --> 00:34:50,880
half a month ago.

721
00:34:50,960 --> 00:34:52,079
During this time,

722
00:34:52,119 --> 00:34:54,360
we've tried to dig deeper into Rujie Law Firm

723
00:34:54,440 --> 00:34:55,599
to find crucial evidence.

724
00:34:56,199 --> 00:34:58,320
We've made contact with senior leaders and junior lawyers.

725
00:34:59,239 --> 00:35:00,079
It's in progress.

726
00:35:00,159 --> 00:35:01,840
We're worried that if we force our way into Rujie,

727
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:03,639
and fail to find the core evidence,

728
00:35:03,639 --> 00:35:06,519
Zhao Yijie will definitely bite back at us,

729
00:35:06,519 --> 00:35:07,719
which would then expose

730
00:35:07,719 --> 00:35:09,360
the existence of our investigation team.

731
00:35:11,079 --> 00:35:11,880
So, Deputy Team Leader,

732
00:35:12,199 --> 00:35:13,679
if we want to investigate Zhao Yijie

733
00:35:13,840 --> 00:35:15,599
or the protective umbrella behind him,

734
00:35:16,400 --> 00:35:18,519
relying on just a few days definitely isn't enough time.

735
00:35:19,440 --> 00:35:20,320
So what?

736
00:35:20,559 --> 00:35:21,840
Everyone, it's been too long.

737
00:35:22,360 --> 00:35:23,880
How much longer do we need to investigate?

738
00:35:23,880 --> 00:35:26,280
How much longer will we let them run rampant?

739
00:35:30,559 --> 00:35:31,199
An ultimatum

740
00:35:32,480 --> 00:35:33,559
has already been issued.

741
00:35:34,320 --> 00:35:36,000
The Chief Procurator verbally notified us

742
00:35:36,440 --> 00:35:37,239
that within three months,

743
00:35:38,559 --> 00:35:40,840
if there is no substantial progress,

744
00:35:44,519 --> 00:35:45,880
our team will no longer exist.

745
00:35:52,320 --> 00:35:56,079
Right now, the fastest way to deliver results is

746
00:35:57,239 --> 00:35:58,320
the Sham Litigation Base.

747
00:36:00,239 --> 00:36:01,599
Can we get Ding Ning on our side?

748
00:36:02,079 --> 00:36:02,920
That would be the fastest.

749
00:36:03,920 --> 00:36:05,159
She just has too strong of a personality.

750
00:36:05,639 --> 00:36:06,840
If we work together,

751
00:36:06,840 --> 00:36:07,960
I'm afraid it might cause unexpected complications.

752
00:36:13,599 --> 00:36:14,320
Forget it.

753
00:36:15,480 --> 00:36:16,880
Whether you and the criminal investigation team

754
00:36:16,880 --> 00:36:19,239
use Liang Zidong to pressure Ding Ning,

755
00:36:19,559 --> 00:36:20,800
or talk to Ding Ning directly,

756
00:36:20,840 --> 00:36:23,679
I just want the location of the Sham Litigation Base.

757
00:36:23,760 --> 00:36:24,519
The sooner, the better.

758
00:36:25,960 --> 00:36:27,760
That's it. Meeting adjourned.

759
00:36:33,400 --> 00:36:34,079
Prosecutor Lei,

760
00:36:34,639 --> 00:36:36,199
please notify the criminal investigation team

761
00:36:36,400 --> 00:36:37,800
to have Liang Zidong request a meeting,

762
00:36:37,880 --> 00:36:38,880
and call Ding Ning over.

763
00:36:39,400 --> 00:36:40,400
Alright. No problem.

764
00:37:09,079 --> 00:37:10,000
Thanks.

765
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:11,360
For coming over in the middle of the night.

766
00:37:13,360 --> 00:37:14,840
The Sham Litigation Base I asked you to find...

767
00:37:14,840 --> 00:37:15,840
It's been so many days.

768
00:37:17,039 --> 00:37:17,880
Have you found it?

769
00:37:17,880 --> 00:37:18,599
I haven't looked.

770
00:37:18,960 --> 00:37:19,719
You haven't?

771
00:37:20,400 --> 00:37:21,079
Why not?

772
00:37:24,599 --> 00:37:26,840
If you have any conditions, just name them.

773
00:37:29,719 --> 00:37:30,760
It's not about conditions.

774
00:37:31,280 --> 00:37:32,280
Then what is it about?

775
00:37:32,800 --> 00:37:33,559
Lawyer Ding.

776
00:37:33,840 --> 00:37:35,440
Don't think that just because you found me,

777
00:37:35,519 --> 00:37:37,159
you can ignore my requests.

778
00:37:38,079 --> 00:37:39,320
I can still change lawyers.

779
00:37:41,360 --> 00:37:42,199
Mr. Liang,

780
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:44,239
let me help you recap.

781
00:37:44,519 --> 00:37:45,719
During our first meeting,

782
00:37:45,719 --> 00:37:48,400
you vividly urged me to find the Sham Litigation Base.

783
00:37:48,760 --> 00:37:50,119
In this second meeting,

784
00:37:50,119 --> 00:37:52,320
you're aggressive, resorting to provocation.

785
00:37:52,559 --> 00:37:53,280
Throughout this entire process,

786
00:37:53,280 --> 00:37:54,920
you haven't asked a single question about your family.

787
00:37:54,920 --> 00:37:55,679
Nor have you asked

788
00:37:55,679 --> 00:37:57,559
about the usual sentencing for your charges.

789
00:37:58,199 --> 00:38:00,079
It seems that besides this Sham Litigation Base,

790
00:38:00,079 --> 00:38:01,400
you don't care about anything else.

791
00:38:02,199 --> 00:38:03,960
Just now, you blamed me for not trusting you.

792
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:07,679
But Mr. Liang, do you trust me?

793
00:38:08,280 --> 00:38:10,280
I don't trust you? Would I hand over such a huge...

794
00:38:10,280 --> 00:38:11,079
Let me finish.

795
00:38:15,280 --> 00:38:16,440
I didn't investigate the base

796
00:38:18,719 --> 00:38:20,880
because I've recently been looking into what you went through.

797
00:38:21,119 --> 00:38:22,519
I went to the bar you frequent

798
00:38:22,519 --> 00:38:23,639
and checked the surveillance footage.

799
00:38:24,039 --> 00:38:26,400
Sure enough, I found that a month before your arrest,

800
00:38:26,559 --> 00:38:28,440
you were already in contact with the prosecutor's office.

801
00:38:28,880 --> 00:38:30,320
I didn't have time to finish watching it

802
00:38:30,559 --> 00:38:31,719
before I went to see my friend.

803
00:38:32,880 --> 00:38:33,719
But I'm guessing

804
00:38:34,519 --> 00:38:36,320
your contact with the prosecutor's office

805
00:38:36,960 --> 00:38:38,760
started even earlier than a month ago, right?

806
00:38:40,119 --> 00:38:42,159
So you didn't suddenly disappear.

807
00:38:42,480 --> 00:38:44,440
You voluntarily turned yourself in

808
00:38:44,440 --> 00:38:45,800
and then put on an act for the public.

809
00:38:46,800 --> 00:38:48,280
And the place you want me to investigate

810
00:38:48,280 --> 00:38:50,159
must be somewhere the prosecutors and the police

811
00:38:50,159 --> 00:38:51,480
both couldn't find.

812
00:38:51,639 --> 00:38:53,280
A place where starting with Zhao Yijie

813
00:38:53,280 --> 00:38:55,719
is the only possible way to find a lead.

814
00:38:57,039 --> 00:38:57,840
Mr. Liang,

815
00:38:58,280 --> 00:39:00,159
even if you don't treat me as a person

816
00:39:00,159 --> 00:39:01,679
and just use me as a tool,

817
00:39:02,440 --> 00:39:04,159
for a place this hard to find,

818
00:39:04,800 --> 00:39:06,960
shouldn't you give me a little more time?
